{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"perplexed-jeanlike-kakarikis","creation_channel":"cli","description":"test_narrow_operation_persists_the_same_bytes_as_the_legacy_sequence (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py) asserts byte-equality between two independently-saved reconciler stores. The saved JSON embeds created_at/updated_at wall-clock timestamps, so when the two save() calls straddle a 1-second boundary the bytes differ (observed on Gerrit change 2209 CI, ubuntu-latest py3.13: 'At index 72 diff: 4 != 3', created_at 06:04:43Z vs 06:04:44Z). Passed on py3.11/py3.12/macos-3.13 in the same run. Root cause: wall-clock dependency the check_wall_clock_asserts gate did not catch. Fix: freeze/inject a fixed clock across both stores' saves so timestamps are deterministic. Discovered while landing olm (MCP client configs); unrelated to that change.","id":"c49a-225d-2bc0-4478","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky wall-clock race in test_rich_reemit_state byte-equivalence test"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787640138248051001,"uuid":"264ecc87-f2d5-4368-9d57-b17616e79493"}